Update to address issues raised with the organization of the code
(header/C file split), typecasting, and use of internal functions
(max/min/abs). Per the thread, I did NOT make any changes to the sysfs
interface. Thanks to Andrew Morton and Greg K-H.

This code has been given a basic test with jstest(1) and appears to
work. However, I won't be able to give it any "live" testing with an
actual game until tomorrow evening, so I'm not yet ready to sign off
on this version of the patch. I will try to have a fully tested
version ready in about 24 hours or so. In the meantime, please let me
know if there are any comments or other needed changes to this patch.

Thanks,
Mike

